&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This solution does not yet exist. Corporate treasury teams must choose between old treasury platforms that fail to support digital assets and crypto-native tools that lack fundamental enterprise treasury elements. You will head the engineering effort to remove this choice by incorporating Ripple&#39;s digital asset abilities into the Ripple Treasury platform in close partnership with Ripple&#39;s core digital assets team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a greenfield role. You will join forces with a seasoned infrastructure engineer and a product lead, forming a team of up to four full-stack developers. The direction may change day-to-day as the team finds what works best. There is no guidebook and no comparable market solution. You will determine how digital assets fit into corporate treasury workflows — and through this, help establish a new category of enterprise software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the engineering process for digital asset integration by building and designing systems that join Ripple&#39;s digital asset functions (XRP, RLUSD, tokenized assets, custody, cross-border settlement) with Ripple Treasury&#39;s enterprise platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a group of up to four full-stack .NET developers, recruiting, mentoring, and developing engineers while staying actively involved in coding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship working software daily — lead a fast-paced Kanban workflow where the team builds, presents, iterates, and adapts direction based on findings and collaborator feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Ripple&#39;s core digital assets team to grasp protocol capabilities, integration points, and roadmap alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design full-stack solutions spanning .NET backend services and Angular or React frontends, ensuring enterprise-grade reliability, security, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity with confidence — make sound engineering decisions with incomplete information, course-correct quickly, and keep the team productive through rapid pivots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, compliance, and treasury domain experts to translate emerging requirements into shippable features that meet the needs of Fortune 500 CFOs and treasurers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define engineering practices for the team — establish coding standards, review processes, testing strategies, and deployment patterns appropriate for a fast-moving, pioneering effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
