&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in São Paulo and reporting to the Managing Director of LatAm, you&#39;ll own a portfolio spanning the Top 50 Banks in Latin America, with a major focus on Brazil, plus strategic capital markets infrastructure accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead the consultative pre-sales motion and close new business across Ripple Core (Ripple Payments, On/Off Ramp, Acceptance Stablecoin/Fiat, OTC, Custody WaaS, Custody Vault, and RLUSD Growth), coordinating with our Ripple Prime and Ripple Treasury business units. You&#39;re the main point of contact for your accounts, working closely with Customer Success, Business Development, Client Solutions, and Partner Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership, quota-carrying role. You should already know these institutions and how to get the meeting. It&#39;s an individual contributor role today; as you bring in revenue, there&#39;s a path to build and lead a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get inside the institution. Understand treasury, FX, ops, capital markets, and compliance pain deeply enough to design a real solution, not run a pitch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline and close, leading with the complete offer rather than a single product, and expand into adjacent products once the first is live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently meet or exceed quarterly targets, with accurate forecasting and clean CRM hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main point of contact and escalation owner, coordinating with Client Solutions, Business Development, Customer Success, Partner Engineering, Ripple Prime, and Ripple Treasury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull in Product, Legal, Compliance, and delivery to solve what the institution actually needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chair quarterly business reviews on Tier 1 accounts, owning deal strategy from discovery through signature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend industry events to expand your network and uncover opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer, feeding insights back to Product and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel frequently across Latin America.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in consultative enterprise sales covering LatAm financial markets, with 5+ years in financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record selling to and sustaining relationships with leading commercial banks and capital markets infrastructure (CSDs, exchanges, clearers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Success selling Enterprise/SaaS through long, complex cycles, leading matrixed deal teams to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grounding in correspondent banking, cross-border payments, and treasury operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to diagnose institutional pain and build the internal case to solve it, not just run a sales process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to connect quickly with decision-makers, including C-suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A comfort in selling a fast-evolving product set whilestaying credible with institutional buyers as it changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Brazil&#39;s regulatory environment for digital assets and payments (BCB, VASP) is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, Portuguese, and Spanish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to have: an existing network of relationships across the LatAm banking industry; familiarity with the digital asset services space (Payments, Custody, Stablecoins, RWA).&lt;/p&gt;
