&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a dedicated, passionate, and eager Senior Staff Technical Program Manager to join our team responsible for leading Ripple&#39;s Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) migration program. This is a challenging and technical role, requiring the expertise to synthesize business and technical requirements and the foresight to ensure we are solving for Ripple&#39;s current and future security needs ahead of Q-Day. You will work closely with InfoSec, XRPL Core, Payments, Custody, Stablecoin, Platform, Compliance, and Legal to drive a company-wide cryptographic migration across asymmetric ciphers, symmetric ciphers, hashing functions, and digital signatures. You will partner with InfoSec on the high-level strategy, but also know when to get hands-on to push an initiative forward. You must be passionate about enabling teams to invent and deliver security-focused solutions to bold and ambiguous challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution of Ripple&#39;s PQC program end-to-end, from cryptographic asset inventory through risk prioritization, tradeoff analysis, and migration execution, against a Q-Day-readiness target of the end of 2028.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up and own a cross-org PQC working group with named owners across XRPL Core, Payments, Custody, Stablecoin, Platform, and InfoSec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment with vendors and partners (custody partners, exchanges, payment processors, HSM vendors) on compatible PQC roadmaps, escalating gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce ambiguity and risk by proactively identifying and eliminating bottlenecks and obstacles, raising issues strategically, and making sound data-driven decisions that deliver for our customers based on associated trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, risk, and progress with purpose and clarity to engineering leadership and executive sponsors, including maintaining the program dashboard reviewed monthly by execs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a role model and an inspiring leader for other TPMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create technical frameworks that can be used by engineering teams for decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence &amp;amp; improve the efficiency of Operational Excellence processes org-wide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with program managers, product managers, and engineering managers to understand development priorities and drive alignment across multiple partners with impactful priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate testing and release dependencies for assigned engineering teams, and across teams as products converge for release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build migration-progress, risk-register, and readiness dashboards to advise partners and leadership of progress and gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of program management experience on initiatives involving sophisticated enterprise tech environments, working directly with many teams across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of cryptographic fundamentals (asymmetric/symmetric ciphers, hashing, digital signatures) sufficient to synthesize technical tradeoffs with engineering and InfoSec stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to PQC, cryptographic migrations, or security/compliance-driven technical programs is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use data and analytics to look at trends and lead health of projects and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coordinate multi-functionally, build consensus, and execute across teams. Able to influence without authority, negotiate, and encourage others in a matrixed environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Jira and Confluence, and proficiency in Google Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience crafting or architecting (design patterns, reliability and scaling) of new and existing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Payments, Custody, Stablecoin, and/or Blockchain ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
